═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§ THEORETICAL-NOTES ← §§ depth-hints
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Ed25519 implementation :
    reference : RFC 8032 + TweetNaCl (~300 LOC C)
    curve     : edwards25519 (2y² = x² + cx²y² form)
    scalar-multiplication : Montgomery ladder for-constant-time
    hash      : SHA-512 (depend-chain)
    trap      : non-constant-time OP leaks key ← use conditional-move
  SHA-256 implementation :
    reference : FIPS 180-4 (~200 LOC)
    block-size: 64 bytes • 64-round compression
    32-bit ops: rotations + AND + XOR + add-mod-2³²
    trap      : endian-conversion ← big-endian for-output
  SHA-512 implementation :
    reference : FIPS 180-4 (~250 LOC)
    block-size: 128 bytes • 80-round compression
    64-bit ops: rotations + AND + XOR + add-mod-2⁶⁴
  Levenshtein :
    Wagner-Fischer : O(mn) time + space
    space-optimization : O(min(m,n)) with two-row technique
    Apocky-notation-distance sometimes-matters for-morpheme-suggest
  Daemon-mode subprocess :
    llama-perplexity.exe likely-no-interactive-mode built-in
    alternative : llama-cli --log-probs + perplexity-compute-in-Python
    OR : llama-server HTTP-endpoint + JSON-RPC
    recommend : try interactive-flag first • fall-back to-server
  Audit-chain legacy-compat :
    entry-schema versioning : add "v":2 field
    verify-tool : dispatch on-v-field
    v1 entries (Python-only signed) ← Odin-tool verifies via-TweetNaCl-equiv
    v2 entries (model+binary SHA) ← requires-new-fields
  SHA-based model-pinning :
    compute-at-load ← amortize over-21-measurements
    cache at ~/.cslv3-m2-models/ with computed-sha sidecar
    re-check only-if mtime changed

